  ],
  "text": "You are the only primate walking around basically naked. That was an upgrade. Every other primate carries a full coat, and a coat is very good at keeping heat in. A furred animal dumps heat by panting, and it can only pant properly once it stops. You dump heat by sweating, and sweat keeps working while you are still moving. Bare skin plus two million sweat glands is a cooling system nothing else out there had. So early humans hunted by simply refusing to stop. An antelope outruns you easily over one kilometre. Over thirty, it overheats and gives up. You are mediocre at almost every other physical measure. Strength, speed, climbing, biting. But you can outlast nearly anything alive. That is what the fur bought. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
